  "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nHow it gets there: `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`. That builds the key as `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`.\n\nRunning the code confirmed it: it returned `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` builds keys the same way but uses the `MET` prefix and never writes to the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
